{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>דָּן יָדִין וְגוֹ׳.</b> Perhaps, since Shimshon said (Judges 16:30) ״תָּמוֹת נַפְשִׁי עִם פְּלִשְׁתִּים״, therefore Jacob said that he is in the category of the judges of Israel who are singled out on high without distinction, and his righteousness should not be diminished. And this is his saying <b>כְּאַחַד שִׁבְטֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל</b> — meaning, like the singular one singled out in every single tribe of Israel, for all the tribes had among them judges for Israel."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:50:34.885928926Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}